Practical No. 10
Layered Microservice Architecture – RestController + Service + JPA Repository
Textbook Reference: Chapter 6 — Building RESTful Microservices
Objective
Structure a RESTful microservice into the standard Controller–Service–Repository layers, keeping business
logic out of the controller and persistence access out of the service. The project uses Spring Boot, Spring
Data JPA, Maven, and an embedded H2 database.
Project Setup Summary
Build tool: Maven | Framework: Spring Boot | Database: H2 (in-memory) | Base package:
com.example.productapi
Package layout: entity, repository, service, controller — each class below belongs to the
package named in its filename bar.
