Notes for Testing
• Set the Postman request header Content-Type: application/json for POST and PUT calls.
• Save each request into a Collection and use {{baseUrl}} as a Postman environment variable (e.g.
http://localhost:8080) so the collection is reusable across environments.
• The H2 console (/h2-console) can be used alongside Postman to visually confirm that
CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE requests are reflected in the PRODUCTS table.
How to Run
1. Place the files in the package structure shown above.
2. Run mvn spring-boot:run (or run ProductApiApplication from an IDE).
3. The API is available at http://localhost:8080/api/products.
4. Open http://localhost:8080/h2-console and connect with JDBC URL
jdbc:h2:mem:productdb, username sa, empty password.
5. Execute the Postman requests from the table above in order: POST → GET (all) → GET (by id) → PUT →
DELETE.
